Legacy Loan Calculator – Refactored Version (Assignment 2)

This project is part of Software Engineering – Assignment 2, where we take an old legacy C++ loan/EMI calculator and modernize it using software-engineering practices.
The original project was forked from:

https://github.com/bradyallenjohnson/LoanCalculatorCpp


The objective is to identify bugs, refactor code, add testing, implement configuration reading, and generate documentation using Doxygen.


Project Features

1)Calculates EMI (Equal Monthly Installment)
2)Handles loan amount, interest rate, and tenure
3)Command-line input handling
4)Refactored into multiple files (Loan.cpp, Loan.h, main.cpp)
5)Added input validation
6)Uses safer numeric types (long double)
7)Reads default values from config.txt
8)GoogleTest unit tests for EMI, invalid input, and large tenures
9)Fully documented using Doxygen
10)Git version controlled with master + dev workflow



Project Structure:
legacy-calc-2009/
├── src/
│   ├── main.cpp
│   ├── Loan.cpp
│   └── Loan.h
│
├── test/
│   └── test_emi.cpp
│
├── config.txt
├── docs/           ← Doxygen-generated documentation
├── Doxyfile
├── README.md
└── REPORT.pdf


Bug Fixes Implemented

1.Input Validation Added
2.Prevents negative/invalid loan amounts
3.Prevents interest rate ≤ 0
4.Prevents tenure ≤ 0
5.Integer Overflow Fix
6.Replaced int/float with long double
7.Used safe math functions (powl())
8.Hardcoded Values Removed
9.Program now loads defaults from config.txt

Refactoring Improvements

1.Split the single main.cpp into modules
2.Created a Loan class in separate header/source files
3.Better formatted output using consistent std::cout
4.Improved command-line argument handling

